issues.what_breaks:
simulate_member! samples z from the chain, independently of the given TX. TN then reads ε^TX computed from the given TX under that sampled z. Under the joint model p(z | TX) ≠ p(z):
- a heatwave TX path is paired with wet regimes;
- the recomputed TX innovations are far from N(0,1) under the wrong regime's μ_k and ρ_k;
- TN = TX − G⁻¹(Φ(rε + …)) takes extreme quantiles;
- RR and the other children of z ignore the information in TX.
